        "original_id": "0ded14b9-ce41-5192-9cfe-21b488ae7841",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick Carpentier\n- Organizations: NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, Go FAS Racing, CART\n- Products: Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, Mercury Milan\n- Places: Ford Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant\n- Events: 1997 CART season, 1997 Marlboro 500\n- Concepts: Rookie of the Year, CD3 platform\n\nFacts:\n- Patrick Carpentier was born on August 13, 1971, and he is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\n- Patrick Carpentier was the Rookie of the Year in the 1997 CART season.\n- The 1997 Marlboro 500 was the 17th and final round of the 1997 CART season.\n- The Ford Fusion was introduced for the 2006 model year.\n- The Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant.\n- The Ford Fusion shares the CD3 platform with the Lincoln MKZ and formerly with the discontinued Mercury Milan.\n- Patrick Carpentier currently competes part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series.\n- Patrick Carpentier drives the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
